---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Krallice — About" description="About Krallice.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-center font-display text-5xl font-medium text-stone-100 md:text-6xl">
      About
    </h1>

    <div class="notes mt-12">
      <p>
        Krallice is Mick Barr, Colin Marston, Nicholas McMaster, Lev Weinstein, and sometimes Dave Edwardson.
        The members have played a different instruments depending on the era of the band. The group has been active since July 2007.
      </p>

      <h2>A note on “initiated”</h2>
      <p>
        “Initiated” means that the songs were written by that person as
        full-length compositions on the instrument they play, be it guitar, bass, or
        synth. The way Krallice songs are mostly written is that a person initiates by
        writing and recording that single-instrument composition, and then everyone
        else writes their own part longitudinally over the entire piece. There are
        cases where one of us has written out a complete multi-part piece from the
        start and given those to the band members, in this case “written” is given as
        the credit. But even in this case the individual player can be assumed to have
        changed the part received somewhat to fit their own musical ergonomics and
        taste.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
